# Part 1: Database (Supabase PostgreSQL)

## 🧠 What is Supabase?

Supabase is a **hosted PostgreSQL database** with a nice web dashboard. Think of it as:
- A **Google Sheets** for your app's data, but way more powerful
- Your data lives on a **server in Mumbai** (`ap-south-1`), close to your users

Your Supabase project: `cgekqqvbipbpduwcapnr`

---

## 1.1 — How to Access Your Database

### Option A: Supabase Dashboard (Easiest)
1. Go to [https://supabase.com/dashboard](https://supabase.com/dashboard)
2. Log in → Select your project (`cgekqqvbipbpduwcapnr`)
3. Click **Table Editor** (left sidebar) — see all 16 tables visually
4. Click **SQL Editor** (left sidebar) — run raw SQL queries

### Option B: From Your Code
Your backend connects automatically via the `DATABASE_URL` environment variable:
```
postgresql://postgres.cgekqqvbipbpduwcapnr:Kishan%40123%402026@aws-1-ap-south-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
```

Broken down:
| Part | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `postgresql://` | Protocol (like `https://` for websites) |
| `postgres.cgekqqvbipbpduwcapnr` | Username (includes your project ID) |
| `Kishan%40123%402026` | Password (`Kishan@123@2026`, URL-encoded) |
| `aws-1-ap-south-1.pooler.supabase.com` | Server address (Mumbai) |
