## 1.2 — Understanding Your Tables

Your database has **16 tables**. Here's what each one does:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[stores] --> B[users]
    A --> C[categories]
    A --> D[products]
    A --> E[bills]
    A --> F[customers]
    A --> G[suppliers]
    A --> H[subscriptions]
    A --> I[notifications]
    A --> J[audit_trails]
    A --> K[daily_summaries]
    A --> L[agent_logs]
    E --> M[bill_items]
    E --> N[print_jobs]
    E --> O[handwritten_bills]
    G --> P[purchase_orders]
```

| Table | Purpose | Key Columns |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| `stores` | Each shop/kadai | name, address, gst_number |
| `users` | Shop owners, managers, cashiers | email, role (OWNER/MANAGER/CASHIER) |
| `products` | Items sold in the shop | name, selling_price, current_stock |
| `categories` | Product categories (Groceries, Snacks...) | name, icon, color |
| `bills` | Sales transactions | total_amount, payment_method, status |
| `bill_items` | Individual items in a bill | product_name, quantity, unit_price |
| `customers` | Customer records | name, phone, credit, loyalty_points |
| `suppliers` | Vendors who supply products | name, phone, pending_amount |
| `purchase_orders` | Orders placed to suppliers | items (JSON), amount, status |
| `subscriptions` | SaaS plan for each store | plan_name, max_products, status |
| `daily_summaries` | End-of-day sales summary | total_revenue, total_bills |
| `notifications` | In-app alerts | title, message, is_read |
| `audit_trails` | Who did what and when | action, old_values, new_values |
| `agent_logs` | AI agent activity logs | agent_name, decision, success |
| `handwritten_bills` | OCR scanned bills | image_path, extracted_data |
| `print_jobs` | Thermal printer queue | bill_id, status, attempts |

