## 1.3 — Common SQL Operations (Supabase SQL Editor)

### 📖 READ data (SELECT)

```sql
-- See all stores
SELECT * FROM stores;

-- See all products in store 1
SELECT name, selling_price, current_stock FROM products WHERE store_id = 1;

-- See today's bills
SELECT * FROM bills WHERE bill_date::date = CURRENT_DATE;

-- See low stock products (below alert threshold)
SELECT name, current_stock, min_stock_alert 
FROM products 
WHERE current_stock < min_stock_alert AND store_id = 1;

-- Count total revenue today
SELECT SUM(total_amount) as today_revenue 
FROM bills 
WHERE store_id = 1 AND bill_date::date = CURRENT_DATE;
```

### ✏️ CREATE data (INSERT)

```sql
-- Add a new product
INSERT INTO products (store_id, name, selling_price, current_stock, unit)
VALUES (1, 'Parle-G Biscuit', 10.00, 100, 'packets');

-- Add a new category
INSERT INTO categories (store_id, name, icon, color)
VALUES (1, 'Snacks', '🍪', '#FF9800');
```

### 🔄 UPDATE data

```sql
-- Update product price
UPDATE products SET selling_price = 12.00 WHERE id = 5;

-- Mark bill as cancelled
UPDATE bills SET status = 'CANCELLED' WHERE id = 10;

-- Reduce stock after sale
UPDATE products SET current_stock = current_stock - 2 WHERE id = 5;
```

### 🗑️ DELETE data

```sql
-- Delete a product (careful!)
DELETE FROM products WHERE id = 99;

-- Soft delete a customer (better practice — keeps the record)
UPDATE customers SET is_active = FALSE, deleted_at = NOW() WHERE id = 5;
```

