## 1.7 — Connection Pooling (Why It Matters)

Your database can only handle a limited number of simultaneous connections. **Connection pooling** reuses connections instead of creating new ones:

```
Without pooling:        With pooling:
Request 1 → New conn    Request 1 ─┐
Request 2 → New conn    Request 2 ─┤→ Shared pool (1-3 connections)
Request 3 → New conn    Request 3 ─┘
(3 connections!)        (1 connection reused!)
```

Your serverless config in [database.py](file:///c:/Users/lalit/Desktop/kadaigpt-main/kadaigpt-main/backend/app/database.py):
```python
"pool_size": 1,       # Keep 1 connection alive
"max_overflow": 2,    # Allow 2 more under heavy load
"pool_recycle": 300,  # Refresh connection every 5 minutes
```

