# Part 3: Quick Reference Cheat Sheet

## Database Cheat Sheet

```sql
-- 🔍 Find something
SELECT * FROM products WHERE name ILIKE '%rice%';  -- case-insensitive search

-- 📊 Count rows
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bills WHERE store_id = 1;

-- 📅 Filter by date range
SELECT * FROM bills 
WHERE store_id = 1 
AND created_at BETWEEN '2026-05-01' AND '2026-05-31';

-- 🔗 Join tables (bills with their items)
SELECT b.bill_number, bi.product_name, bi.quantity, bi.total
FROM bills b
JOIN bill_items bi ON bi.bill_id = b.id
WHERE b.store_id = 1
ORDER BY b.created_at DESC
LIMIT 20;

-- 📈 Top selling products
SELECT product_name, SUM(quantity) as total_sold, SUM(total) as total_revenue
FROM bill_items bi
JOIN bills b ON b.id = bi.bill_id
WHERE b.store_id = 1
GROUP BY product_name
ORDER BY total_sold DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

## Vercel Cheat Sheet

| Task | How |
|------|-----|
| Deploy | `git push origin main` (auto) or `vercel --prod` |
| View logs | Vercel Dashboard → Logs |
| Add env variable | Dashboard → Settings → Environment Variables |
| Check status | `curl .../api/ping` |
| API docs | `https://kadaigpt-main.vercel.app/api/docs` |
| Redeploy | Dashboard → Deployments → Redeploy |
| Preview deploy | Push to a non-main branch |

## File Structure That Matters

```
kadaigpt-main/
├── api/
│   ├── index.py              ← Vercel entry point (bridges to FastAPI)
│   ├── requirements.txt      ← Python packages for Vercel
│   └── .python-version       ← Python 3.12
├── backend/
│   └── app/
│       ├── main.py            ← FastAPI app (routes, middleware, CORS)
│       ├── database.py        ← DB connection (pooling, SSL, health checks)
│       ├── config.py          ← Settings (reads env variables)
│       ├── models/            ← SQLAlchemy models (Python ↔ DB tables)
│       └── routers/           ← API endpoints (auth, bills, products...)
├── frontend/
│   ├── src/                   ← React source code
│   └── dist/                  ← Built files (Vercel serves these)
├── vercel.json                ← Vercel config (routing, regions, limits)
└── setup_tables_v2.sql        ← Database schema (run in Supabase SQL Editor)
```

